  "statement": "For the hash-pinned A1 production coefficients and A10-A13 strict sharp cubes, all prior A13 reductions remain binding at T4. R-079 closes the exact expectation-level full frame-current and canonical safe-packet Doob decomposition left open by R-078: one conditional low-current block, present-control increments, and future-control innovations reconstruct the complete endpoint, with the present/future cross term, positive squares, covariance traces, paid endpoint difference, and complete low endpoint retained. It proves a spatially weighted Cameron--Martin control square function that spends strict-past control energy once and an exact backward-heat projection for the base or predictably translated current. The terminal future-feedback current still has coefficient and derivative-feedback commutators. Generic Cauchy, expected-budget-to-BMO, abstract spatial-gain, and adapted Wick carre-du-champ shortcuts fail. The production near/far current-trace bound, separate low-object bounds, complete packet lower bound, controlled-shell one-use, and q=10/9 Nelson theorem remain open.",
