  "notes": "Scoped T4 exact/analytic reduction plus executed adversarial diagnostics. A13-CLASSII-FULL-SAFE-PACKET-FRAME-CURRENT-DOOB-DECOMPOSITION (R-079) closes the exact expectation-level algebraic gap left by R-078: the complete frame-current endpoint splits into the conditional low-current block, present-control increments, and future-control innovations, with the cross term, positive squares, simultaneous Wick traces, paid endpoint difference, and complete low endpoint retained. It proves one weighted Cameron--Martin square-function use for the control coordinate and the backward-heat projection for a base or predictably translated current. The terminal feedback current still contains coefficient and derivative-feedback channels. Generic weighted Cauchy has deficit -4/15; expected budgets do not imply conditional BMO; generic spatial gain and adapted Wick carre-du-champ positivity fail. These are method no-gos, not production counterexamples. Primary 51/51, non-importing independent 42/42, integrated 157/157, and aggregate 250/250 pass. The final ten-page PDF has zero overfull boxes, no forms, and page-by-page visual QA. T-050 remains in progress at the production near/far current-trace estimate, separate low-object bounds, complete packet lower bound, controlled-shell one-use, and Nelson synthesis. Tier stays T4."
